    "text": {
     "en": "On National Cleanliness Day children and their teacher clean the park.\nHave you seen piles of waste near your home or school? How is waste created?\nIn our everyday activities we create a lot of waste: old clothes, tins, bottles, paper, peels of vegetables and fruits, plastic wrappers, pencil shavings and old batteries.\nWaste ends up in garbage piles if we throw it carelessly.\nManaging waste is in our own hands.\nKeep wet waste, like peels and leftovers, separate from dry waste, like paper, plastic and tins."
    }
